<!--
  Pioneer DJ DDJ-400: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    DDJ-400 List of MIDI messages version 1.00 (Pioneer DJ (now AlphaTheta Corporation), 2018-05-16 (PDF date)), pages 1-3
    https://downloads.support.alphatheta.com/software_info/dj-controllers/DDJ-400/DDJ-400_MIDI_Message_List_E1.pdf
    DDJ-400 MIDI-compatible software (links the list above) (AlphaTheta Help Center, accessed 2026-11-07), pages n/a
    https://support.alphatheta.com/en-US/articles/4405094309657
    DDJ-400 Operating Instructions (DRI1551B) (Pioneer DJ (now AlphaTheta Corporation), 2022-07-19 (PDF date)), pages 6-7 (CUE/LOOP CALL halves/doubles; RELOOP/EXIT; IN/4BEAT), 15 (Beat Loop and Beat Jump pads), 19 (Utilities mode, general MIDI controller), 21 (MIDI device name), 23 (other DJ applications)
    https://downloads.support.alphatheta.com/manuals/dj-controllers/DDJ-400/DDJ-400_DRI1551B_manual.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.

  BEFORE YOU START: When rekordbox is not running, the unit works as a general MIDI controller and sends these messages. To force general MIDI mode even while rekordbox is running: disconnect USB, hold SHIFT + left-deck PLAY/PAUSE while you connect USB (Utilities mode), press the left-deck BEAT JUMP mode button so it is lit, then disconnect USB (manual p. 19). AlphaTheta's help page also says to power-cycle the unit after you switch DJ applications.

  CADENCE'S CHOICES:
    the jog is the platter TOP's turn with Vinyl mode on (CC 34), the unit's default. With Vinyl mode off the top sends CC 35, and the wheel's side sends its own message: Learn either to the jog row if that is how you play.
    Not bound, because one target holds one control: Deck 1 CUE button (ch1.cuepad1), since Deck 1 PAD 1, HOT CUE mode takes ch1.cuepad1; Deck 2 CUE button (ch2.cuepad1), since Deck 2 PAD 1, HOT CUE mode takes ch2.cuepad1.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): SHIFT button (note 63) and all +SHIFT messages; Jog touch (note 54), jog wheel side turn (CC 33), jog turn with Vinyl mode off (CC 35), SHIFT+jog (CC 41); LOOP IN/4BEAT (note 16; long press note 20) and LOOP OUT (note 17): no loop-in/out target; RELOOP/EXIT feeds chN.loop; BEAT SYNC long press (note 92); TEMPO slider (CC 0/32), TRIM (CC 4/36), crossfader (ch 7 CC 31/63); MASTER CUE button (ch 7 note 99); Beat FX section: BEAT ◀/▶, BEAT FX SELECT, CH SELECT, LEVEL/DEPTH, ON/OFF; Pad mode buttons (HOT CUE 27, BEAT LOOP 109, BEAT JUMP 32, SAMPLER 34 on ch 1/2); BEAT LOOP pads 5-8; BEAT JUMP pads 3-8; SAMPLER, KEYBOARD, PAD FX 1/2, KEY SHIFT pad pages; Fader start notes (102, 82), channel level meter, and the MIDI-OUT settings (LOADED, LEVEL METER, VINYL MODE, FADER START, CROSSFADER REV., CUT LAG, BACK SPIN)

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
<CadenceMidiMap name="Pioneer DJ DDJ-400" maker="Pioneer DJ" model="DDJ-400" match="ddj400" version="1">
  <bind target="ch1.clip" kind="1" ch="1" num="11" status="manual"/>  <!-- Deck 1 PLAY/PAUSE, p. 1 -->
